Z||000007||ChadMan||11-28-1999||08:41 AM||||Wow, a notchback Fiero!  It's looking good.  Did you start from a C4 Corvette, Overlord?  What engine will you use?<P>Four50four, I'm using the stock settings that came with Arroyo's Fiero.  I think the key to low lap times at Hometown is to keep your speed up on the long downhill run from the covered bridges into town, then powerslide through the two 90-degree bends in town.<P>I think I'm pretty fast at Hometown and Atlantica, but Rocky Pass and Summit still give me fits.  Any tips?||||reg||14
Z||000008||four50four||11-28-1999||10:36 AM||||i figured out why i was so slow! my pedels weren't calibrated properly, so when i had my foot to the floor, it would only run at 3/4 throttle. its like somebody added a supercharger to every car!||||reg||3
Z||000009||chris6878||11-28-1999||09:51 PM||||Hometown: 1:24:87<BR>Redrock Ridge: 2:23:68<BR>Atlantica: 2:19:65<BR>Rocky Pass: 2:52:59<BR>Country Woods: 2:45:18<BR>Lost Canyons: 3:00:26<BR>Aquatica: 2:51:06<BR>Summit:  i havent beat the computers lap time<P>I am also racing the same fiero as Chadman... but its slightly modified, i brighened the side marker lights and tinkered with the running part of it... i used the VivWizard.  This allows u to take the cars in ther respective folder,   and break down the  "car.viv". Its kind of like a winzip file... its about 10 files compressed into one and the vivWizard will extract them for u..         The file called "Carp.txt"  is the one where u modify the performance. U can also tinker with the dash and the external parst of the cars with the different files.      On my car i didnt do anything with the handling, so it still handles good as a fiero   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">       but runs like one with a heavily modified v8.. i have topped it at 203  mph one time...    the highest it usually get is 185 - 190 ..   but if u get on the right strectch of road.. who knows?           sorry my post was so long...     happy racing...<P>chris||||reg||6
